 $tan⁡x=\\frac{1}{3},$ we get that $tan⁡(x+5\\pi )=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n12tan⁡(x+5\\pi )-6=12(\\frac{1}{3})-6=4-6=-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eed0c7c3-0bb5-56eb-a9ca-9ec4dc7b3efe" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a2efa17-ff90-5110-b52d-af24637f4842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235979} {:answer/id #uuid "2f8cca99-6d65-568c-a0f8-a0fd7fe46ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236118} {:answer/id #uuid "707b921b-1acb-53f3-8f3a-b5470f3888af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12-3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236530} {:answer/id #uuid "a845e9d4-c867-568d-aa25-63440fc514dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236870} {:answer/id #uuid "aa563b5d-37dd-55e3-947b-a55588cc5905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f8cca99-6d65-568c-a0f8-a0fd7fe46ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236118} :answer-field/id #uuid "14995e9f-f94a-5811-a957-cbe2b6653873" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89698ed1-75aa-53ec-b284-4e5a8a12ecbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-103312" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=16,$ for some value of $x,$ find the value of $\\frac{3}{4}tan⁡(x-9\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\